PHASE 6B — VERIFY AND IMPLEMENT ACTUAL MCP PROTOCOL

We have completed the banking service layer and currently have endpoints under:

/mcp/Tools/...

However, before proceeding to RAG/Azure AI Search, verify whether NovaBanking.McpServer is actually implementing the Model Context Protocol (MCP), or whether it is only exposing ordinary ASP.NET Core REST controller endpoints.

IMPORTANT:
Do not assume that an ASP.NET controller called "McpToolsController" is an MCP implementation.

Inspect the current codebase and determine whether the project:
- implements an actual MCP server
- exposes MCP tools through an MCP-compatible transport/protocol
- uses an appropriate .NET MCP SDK/package
- exposes tool metadata/schema in the MCP format
- supports MCP tool discovery/invocation

If the current implementation is only REST endpoints, convert the MCP server to a genuine MCP implementation while preserving the existing secure architecture.

==================================================
REQUIRED MCP TOOLS
==================================================

Expose these actual MCP tools:

GetCustomerProfile()
GetAccountSummary()
GetAccountBalance(accountId)
GetRecentTransactions(accountId, count)
GetLoanSummary(loanId)
GetCreditCardSummary(cardId)

Do NOT add:
- transfers
- payments
- card blocking
- PIN changes
- credit decisions
- account mutations
- loan mutations
- credit-card mutations

==================================================
SECURITY
==================================================

CRITICAL:

The LLM/MCP caller must NEVER supply CustomerId as an authorization identity.

CustomerId must continue to come from authenticated server-side context.

The MCP tool must call the existing IBankingService.

The architecture must remain:

MCP Tool
    ↓
IBankingService
    ↓
ICurrentUserAccessor
    ↓
authenticated server-side session
    ↓
CustomerId
    ↓
ownership predicate
    ↓
Azure SQL

Do NOT:
- query EF Core directly from MCP
- accept CustomerId as a tool parameter
- trust CustomerId from the LLM
- hardcode CustomerId
- bypass BankingService
- bypass ownership checks
- replace server-side sessions with JWTs
- weaken authentication

==================================================
AUTHENTICATED CONTEXT
==================================================

The existing architecture uses NB_SID.

Inspect how the MCP server receives authenticated context.

If the MCP server receives the NB_SID cookie directly, validate it server-side exactly as the existing CurrentUserAccessor does.

If actual MCP transport does not naturally support the existing cookie/session mechanism, DO NOT create a security bypass.

Instead implement the minimal server-side authenticated bridge/context necessary to preserve:

"CustomerId is derived from authenticated server-side state."

Document the exact mechanism.

Never allow the MCP client or LLM to choose the customer identity.

==================================================
MCP TOOL DEFINITIONS
==================================================

Each tool needs:
- tool name
- clear description
- parameter schema where applicable
- read-only behavior
- safe structured output

Tool parameters:

GetCustomerProfile:
No parameters.

GetAccountSummary:
No parameters.

GetAccountBalance:
accountId

GetRecentTransactions:
accountId
count

GetLoanSummary:
loanId

GetCreditCardSummary:
cardId

Resource IDs are only resource selectors.

They are NOT authorization credentials.

